// Brute-force sign-in detection - MITRE ATT&CK T1110
// Detects 4+ failed sign-ins followed by a success, same source IP and
// account, clustered within a 5-minute window. Runs against synthetic
// telemetry in SyntheticSignins_CL for this home-lab exercise.
//
// Used as the scheduled query behind the "Synthetic Brute Force Sign-In
// Detection" Sentinel analytics rule (MITRE: Credential Access / T1110).
//
// Schedule: every 1 hour, lookback 1 hour, so each event is evaluated by
// exactly one run. The last line returns the event time as TimeGenerated so
// the alert reflects when the activity happened.

SyntheticSignins_CL
| where TimeGenerated > ago(1h)
| summarize
    FailedAttempts = countif(ResultType == "Failure"),
    SuccessAttempts = countif(ResultType == "Success"),
    TotalAttempts = count(),
    FirstFailure = minif(TimeGenerated, ResultType == "Failure"),
    LastEvent = max(TimeGenerated)
    by SourceIP, UserPrincipalName
| extend TimeSpan = LastEvent - FirstFailure
| where TimeSpan < 5m and FailedAttempts >= 4 and SuccessAttempts >= 1
| extend TimeGenerated = LastEvent
